{"title":"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Similar_to_[1])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Similar to [1])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(non_trig_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(non trig solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The angles in a particular triangle are in arithmetic progression, and the side lengths are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba093ec86ee0e3f1ec47f613cb3e343ec7117d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,5,x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. The sum of the possible values of x equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc04c0988983661ce28dfe63bc62dd7054fe93a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+\\sqrt{b}+\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06bfa9bd396251568dafe71019b3e0afe2e49c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 38\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 40\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 42\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the angles are in an arithmetic progression, and the angles add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, the second largest angle in the triangle must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. Also, the side opposite of that angle must be the second longest because of the angle-side relationship. Any of the three sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, could be the second longest side of the triangle.\n</p><p>The law of cosines can be applied to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in all three cases.\n</p><p>When the second longest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/9465cacd4d4df9d863a7341ee82ab2f6ce4c14a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2 = 4^2 + x^2 - 2(4)(x)\\cos 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"19\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71097cc2d61ce1f86e984bb04f4fbea1a8321dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 4x - 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" />. By using the quadratic formula, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6946aae5b83570071ea514fb33415c1036872ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac {4 + \\sqrt{16 + 36}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/7/277126f9f360e116b0783fa5d2ced638d1492c93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2 + \\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>When the second longest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca43996a1dc5bc8e3dc0c3a628103021ec4173d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 5^2 + 4^2 - 40\\cos 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"16\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625a770ff96d2107b3d252be809917684378476e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>When the second longest side is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/7/937b192edd494b61bb592f5727ec9db684178ab4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 = 5^2 + x^2 - 2(5)(x)\\cos 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"231\" height=\"19\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79f8e32de7bc4bba1d0d91729a34284dfdd07c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 5x + 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />. Using the quadratic formula, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f04e943e44ecf131255b65955dcca7e687fb77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac {5 + \\sqrt{25 - 36}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"142\" height=\"40\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/1140d9d5d98d56ed2cc698afbb9c6e0aa6a56fc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{-11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> is not real, therefore the second longest side cannot equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Adding the two other possibilities gets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5acbe2f9e02a06138a1d68acb87dbfbab2e395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + \\sqrt{13} + \\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e0360c1e104b68c54f1a8ef42d50cf6084a637f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 2, b=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5db7c4591c4d909481f9b46bd1d1d25688cf728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/f/c4ffd7566f7be7a56881b638c9f767286e98912f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />, which is answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5bdc2c0e59651ee5e6fa74ba318dc73d744feb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Similar_to_.5B1.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Similar_to_[1])\">Solution 2 (Similar to [1])</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Similar to [1])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The angle measures of the triangle are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72bd374eae1eda72e65eac93f174c805360811a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf73b56f92e336948f160e54b1ff5059d87820cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + 2d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> for some common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through the definition of arithmetic sequence.\n</p><p>Angle sum formula gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a13aadfc7d74ca543a13731d461e805a917cace4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta + 3d = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"16\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0ad33cca5dc31dcdaa3a6b1b33673d1680b4fb66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta+d = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>One inscribed measure of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33ab6763be7cfcf250f0b1f08d141b0aff503b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta + d = 60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. We do casework on where this angle is inscribed, using LoC along the way. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c3991aa1585672ff1601f77d0f74d1f32075e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(60^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is inscribed with 4 and 5, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e714784518d341ecf1d219e9ef67785830ce1563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 41 - 20 = 21 \\implies x = \\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"262\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is inscribed with 5 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b61dfe5ca386baf8d7e22bc081f36e1de59f4d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-9 = x^2 - 5x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/5/11590d9b608acbcf927fc43bebb0c6faa21f1f9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 5x +9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />. No such solutions exist checking the discriminant.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> is inscribed with 4 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3a341e604806faae1694044ed1a819dd49c9e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 = x^2 - 4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71097cc2d61ce1f86e984bb04f4fbea1a8321dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 4x - 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"123\" height=\"15\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/89560a2c1b5ec90bcfeffd4db697aa9557ace2ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{+} = 2+\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" /> is the only correct root that satisfies the properties of Plane Euclidean Geometry. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb6241f654731ae7815fbe2fc2bbae55f0b060a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum \\textbf{all~} x = 2+\\sqrt{13} + \\sqrt{21} \\implies 2 + 13 + 21 = \\boxed{36}\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28non_trig_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(non_trig_solution)\">Solution 3(non trig solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(non trig solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, set the angles equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e4f29951abd9ec55ff36c90415304b86e29fe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b,~a,~a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />. Added together should equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/1490e87657cf31a11efb5a3d5cbeab5a9caba3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3a=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3cbfdcb4acd5efa631f25e5e5bf6334d1e1194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />. So the angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc0cddcff9bc5ba077616e6570c720f1a1658ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60-b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e422477f3b0d34176e93294521826e752c3c4c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> for some number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We already know two of the sides are four and five, so now there are three cases. \n</p><p>1. Four and five are the two sides around the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>2.only the 4 side is touching the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>3. Only 5 side is touching the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Case 1: both 4 side and 5 side touch the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d5c45388de5c75af641c046d466de3592ffa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. Now, draw an altitude from the vertice the 4 side does not share with the five side. It will result in a 30-60-90 triangle with 4 as the hypotenuse, so the part on the. 5 side equals 2 and the height of the triangle, both the 30-60-90 and the whole triangle, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. We have a right triangle from the altitude, the remaining 3 on the 5 side, and the remaining side of the big triangle that we are looking for. By Pythagorean theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710660578b5ca91965903b4e96bf88e35432b218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{3})^2+3^2=21=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"24\" />remaining side squared. So in this case the third side is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b7a75cd4076dc5e9aaed1c570289a4e27802d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Case 2: only 4 side is touching the 60 degrees. Set third side we are looking for as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Once again draw an altitude down, this time from the shared vertice of the 4 and 5 sides to side x. Once again height equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e455d80f4657b1112ba302a6e2c42e9c81f780ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> with an almost exact copy paste of above. Once again the bottom side part is 2 for the 30-60-90 triangle. However this time, the Pythagorean theorem equation we get is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/855ea771aed21105e88d504c1e0b16bb670e22b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{3})^2 + (a-2)^2 =5^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"182\" height=\"24\" />? This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c71742214705a77d3817a9e68b3b55fb0269a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"21\" /> equals 13. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0928ce1f7bd2a717e3a16a2ee34f1deb138a69bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-4a-9=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. Use quadratic formula to get that the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c0644e61fc880df4a3d5ae301c256ed1d38943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />,\n</p>\n<pre><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05eddc241d6495929e44dfb38232f2818e488607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />. Clearly a length must be positive so we discard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05eddc241d6495929e44dfb38232f2818e488607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />. So in case 2, the third side is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05eddc241d6495929e44dfb38232f2818e488607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />.\n</pre>\n<p>Case 3: set unknown third side as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Once again draw an altitude down, this time from the connecting vertice of an and the 4 side to the 5 side. The bottom part on the 5 side equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/f/9afddc3c61aa4e66d003d0c7cc5bd01560d341f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"34\" />, and the height of the triangles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae77670ddf63029489697f26105d93b36b5f84b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"40\" height=\"43\" />. So the Pythagorean equation we receive this time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/77421862a87e4a93970c0500c0951de99cb8fe1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$((\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})a)^2 +(5-\\frac{a}{2})^2 =16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"207\" height=\"43\" />. expanding it out results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/7107e195303507f0db3485ab1703f794f15bf46e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{3}{4})a^2 + 25-5a+\\frac{a^2}{4} =16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"41\" />. Which, simplified, equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be003289c9e93eb47d73896205d838cf7d38f326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-5a+9=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. However, the discriminant is -11 which is clearly less than zero so there are no real roots. If you draw this case out you will realize it is impossible to draw such a triangle. \n</p><p>Thus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfc31d9b07af3cf0877dab720cf8363e666f516d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+\\sqrt{13}+sqrt{21}=a+\\sqrt{b}+\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"23\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/a/8ea5216741095fbad349a2ec93cf6f75faa4e900.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2, b=13, c=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c47466f30ff532f123b93b5edf0915eec22c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+13+21=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" /> which is answer choice A. \n</p><p>~Nyx3.14\n~latex formatting by MegaCleverStarfish15\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XQpQaomC2tA\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XQpQaomC2tA</a>\n</p><p>(NOTE: Problem 12 starts at 8:50 in the youtube video  ~jyang66)\n</p><p>~sugar_rush\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A\">2013 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.p